  {
    "section": "road",
    "claim": "Total road is not a real quantity. Unconditionally it looks like a powerful predictor \u2014 White scores 14% at the bottom of the range and 87% at the top \u2014 but almost all of that is the piece count in disguise, because a side with more pieces has more cobs and so more road. Held at equal material the curve flattens to noise. What matters is not how much road a side owns but whether particular cobs have run out; see the cramp measurements.",
